# {{ brand_name | default('Brand', true) }} — Brand Creative Brief

## 1. Brand Foundation
Core promise, product/service, audience, voice, tone, and values.

## 2. Visual Identity
Exact supplied colors, visual language, and typography. Do not invent ownership of fonts or replace supplied values with generic defaults.

## 3. Creative Assets
Explain that the official logo is the identity anchor; aesthetic references are advisory; exact products, packaging, people, characters, properties, vehicles, or interfaces are required only when depicted as factual.

## 4. Creative Latitude and Boundaries
State what the agency may create freely, mandatory treatments, and prohibited treatments.

## 5. Campaign Truth
Campaign-specific offers, claims, disclosures, and immutable assets come from the active campaign and block only the affected deliverable when missing.

## 6. Governance
Folder authorization permits production use; approval occurs on campaign direction and finished creative; templates are optional for deliberately locked layouts.

Keep the brief concise and practical. Never introduce another brand's colors, terminology, product model, or CTA language.